{
  "case_id": "2011-11-400",
  "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The constitutionality of the Act's massive expansion of Medicaid depends on the answer to two related questions. First, is the expansion coercive? And, second, does that coercion matter?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Clement, can I ask you a -- just a matter of clarification? Would you be making the same argument if, instead of the Federal Government picking up 90 percent of the cost, the Federal Government picked up 100 percent of the cost?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we're also told that there are other States that like this expansion, and they are very glad to have it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there any chance that all 26 States opposing it have Republican governors, and all of the States supporting it have Democratic governors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's a correlation, Justice Scalia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, when does a program become too big? I'd want you to -- give me a dollar number."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "$3.3 trillion over the next 10 years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is the sheer size. Two is the fact that this statute uniquely is tied to an individual mandate which is decidedly nonvoluntary. And three is the fact that they've leveraged the prior participation in the program, notwithstanding that they've broken this out as a separately segregated fund going forward, which is not to prove --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the inevitable consequence of your position was that the Federal Government could just do this on its own, the Federal Government could have Medicaid, Medicare, and these insurance regulations -- assuming that's true -- then how are the interests of federalism concerned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0001-0008",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It's leverage, pure and simple."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The States do not contend otherwise. The States are asking this Court to do something unprecedented, which is to declare this an impermissibly coercive exercise of power."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But there's no coercion question at all?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you recognize any limitation on that concern?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would that be -- would that reach the point -- would that be the point where financial inducement turns into coercion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, General, what's the -- been the history of its use? Has the Secretary in fact ever made use of that authority?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the Arizona letter we just heard about today?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0002-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The first of their three arguments for coercion, the sheer size argument, that it's very difficult to see how that is going to work, because if the question is about what you stand to lose rather than what you stand to gain, then it seems to me that it doesn't matter whether the Medicaid expansion is substantial or whether it's modest, or whether there's any expansion at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is that subsumed in the coercion test, or is that an independent test?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, I'm not following this argument. Take the poorest of the poor. If there is no Medicaid program, then they're not going to get health care. Isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b758ae1dd4ceaa301bd1079981de1800bcfa6f5056072943976a4c99ba180692",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b758ae1dd4ce-0004-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-11-400",
